# fixedbugs, defect 2056, lane land-214, 2026-10-14: what the repair leaves.
#
# `LIMIT` and `EXTRA`, bound from `fixedbugs-2056-second.h`, are macros of a
# file it includes, read once already through `fixedbugs-2056-first.h`'s
# group, so they stand before its own group's header and that header leaves
# them as they were: the shape of an earlier group's macro read in place of
# the header's own. Asked again with the first group left out, the header
# makes them the same, `EXTRA` only because the switch's group is kept,
# so both are the header's own, `7` and `9`, and nothing is refused.

extern "fixedbugs-2056-switch.h"
    constant WANT_EXTRA: i32

extern "fixedbugs-2056-first.h"
    function aye() -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-2056-second.h"
    constant LIMIT: i64
    constant EXTRA: i64
    function bee() -> i32

function main()
    print(LIMIT)
    print(EXTRA)
    print(aye() + bee() + WANT_EXTRA)
